  "status": "published",
  "title": "Solar Shed Lighting Kit",
  "summary": "A 30 W panel, battery and LED strip so the shed has light with no cable from the house.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 5,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Pick the panel spot: the roof or wall facing the equator (south in the northern hemisphere), tilted at roughly your latitude, with no shade from 10 am to 2 pm. The battery is sealed AGM rather than lithium because an unheated shed gets cold, and lithium (LiFePO4) batteries must not be charged below freezing.",
    "Mount the panel on the Z brackets, screwing into rafters or solid sheathing, and seal each screw head.",
    "Drill a hole for a cable gland with the step bit, bring the panel cable in through the gland, and leave a drip loop outside so water runs off before it reaches the hole.",
    "Mount the battery off the floor and the charge controller on the wall right beside it, so the battery leads stay short.",
    "Wire it in this order: battery to controller first, with a fused lead as close to the battery positive as you can (the controller reads the system voltage from the battery). Then connect the panel. Set the controller's battery type to sealed/AGM.",
    "Clean the mounting surface with alcohol and stick the LED strip on. Run its leads through the rocker switch to the controller's load terminals, not straight to the battery: the load output disconnects the lights before the battery is drained flat.",
    "Test with the multimeter: battery voltage at the controller, panel voltage in sun near the open-circuit figure on the panel's label, and the controller showing it is charging. Then switch the lights on.",
    "Clip every cable to the wall about every 12 in so nothing hangs where it can snag."
  ],
